**Summary highlights:** The paper uses affine Weyl group geometry to bound Lusternik-Schnirelmann category via alcove-vertex conjugacy classes. The core technical machinery (sections 04-05) constructs contractible cells that lift to deformation retracts on the Lie group. The SU(n+1) case recovers Singhof's known result. The Sp(n) analysis is most developed, with quaternionic Grassmannian identifications and conjectured bounds; contractibility questions remain open. The Spin cases are structurally identified but lack detailed relative-category analysis.
